<Item XName="VarBlock" Type="VarBlock" /></Item>
<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;H1 class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt&quot;&gt;Narrowband Hybrid Beamforming Architecture&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/H1&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;H2 class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;This example demonstrates a flexible and configurable narrowband hybrid beamforming system. The Digital Modulation&amp;nbsp;source and receiver are used and so the license for DigMod is needed&lt;/STRONG&gt;. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL type=disc&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Supported Features:&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 1. Support flexible beamforming structure, including full digital beamforming, hybrid beamforming and full RF/analog beamforming.&amp;nbsp;&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;2. For hybrid beamforming and full RF/analog beamforming, a reference algorithm model is provided to train beamformer in transmitter and receiver given the ideal channel information.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;3. A 3D MIMO channel is provided supporting use-defined scenario per 3GPP 3D MIMO standard and NYU scenario for mmwave frequency.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;4. Support customer beam pattern import and RF impairment.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Note1&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;All configurations are collected&amp;nbsp;in &quot;Equations&quot;&amp;nbsp;Tab of the schematic and relavant comments are attached following the corresponding settings.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;1. ULA and UPA are supported in y-z plane, which says antenna number in x-axis direction should equals to one.&lt;BR&gt;2. The way to construct the vectors, such as TxPosition_X, TxPosition_Y, TxPosition_Z, TxAntennaArrayMask, TxPhaseShifterDistortion in Tx.As for TxPosition_X, TxPosition_Y and&amp;nbsp;TxPosition_Z, the order of the elements in these vectors&amp;nbsp;are antenna in y-axis first, in z-axis second and in x-axis third. The length of these vectors is Nt. The structure of counterparts in Rx is the same.&amp;nbsp;As for TxAntennaArrayMask, the dimension is Nt-by-Ntrf. The first&amp;nbsp;column corresponds to the connections between the first RF chain and each antenna elements, and the second column corresponds to the connections between the second RF chain and each antenna elements, and so on. The value of each element is 0 or 1. 1 indicates connected and 0 indicates disabled. The structure of counterparts in Rx is the same. As for TxPhaseShifterDistortion, the dimension is also Nt-by-Ntrf. The structure is the same as TxAntennaArrayMask. But the value of each element can be complex which represents the amplitude distortion and phase distortion.&lt;BR&gt;3. The parameter &quot;OSR&quot; is OverSampling Rate which is four&amp;nbsp;in the example.&lt;BR&gt;4. &quot;PathDelay&quot; is a parameter for channel modeling and&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;values in the example are all zero (in terms of seconds). Please&amp;nbsp;keep&amp;nbsp;these values zeros, because&amp;nbsp;only narrowband transmission is supported in this demo. Both reference 2-path and 4-path channel configurations are provided for demonstration. &lt;BR&gt;6. The angle scopes for plotting are [0,180] for zenith and 0,360] for azimuth, so the mirror radiation pattern would show in case of ULA and UPA configuration. The plotting granularity is 1 degree. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL style=&quot;MARGIN-TOP: 0in&quot; type=disc&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Note2&lt;/STRONG&gt;: &lt;BR&gt;1. The DigMod&amp;nbsp;source and receiver only support&amp;nbsp;single RF chain, so&amp;nbsp;the maximum number of RF chains in transmitter and receiver are 1 in this example. The maximum number of antennas in transmitter and receiver is 256.|&lt;BR&gt;2. SubtractionDuetoCH = 0.306dB need subtracted from the signal&apos;s simulation SNR due to the power boost introduced by 3D channel model. Please note that the value is only available in current configuration and it should be adjusted according to the channel configuration (including parameter &quot;Seed&quot; and the number of antennas).&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
